From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:31:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/79] runner: the graph bank, its packets and route.Dispatch

Third slice of the in-thinking runner port, from the DSV41
release branch (7b79ef92d) unchanged except for names: runner_graph*.zig loads
a boot-time bank of precompiled operation and size templates (exact integer,
decimal and rational kernels at width 256: add, sub, mul, div, mod, divmod,
pow, powmod, formatting) and binds a request's literals and rows into packets,
so nothing compiles at request time. steps_v1/ is the frozen step model the
bank's binary format hashes. The frontend's inline integer cells and their
def/list/loop tests come with it.

Build: test-runner-graph-host (in test-cuda-host), rooted at
runner_graph_test.zig; the bank-backed tests skip unless TF_RUNNER_GRAPH_BANK
names a bank. Model-independent; nothing in the engine imports it yet.
